24,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The earth-moving firms are worried about clay and slippage. Big digs look risky, but small work is fine.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"People mostly stick to the firm ground to reach the tram, and the heat is getting quite intense.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Minato,,"We have very few staff left, but there are volunteers for habitat work and sports.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The water basins from years ago are still great, but the paved areas are falling apart quickly.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The habitat fund covers planting and water, but not buildings. Also, greenery is much more expensive to maintain.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if people want firm ground, maybe we shouldn't dig too deep or change the paths too much.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Exactly. And with the drainage issues I found, we need something that handles water better than the current system.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Jonathan, if the habitat fund pays for planting, maybe that helps with the high upkeep costs you mentioned?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Kenji, if the basins held up well, maybe a water-based design is more durable than paving.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"The fund helps the start, but the annual ledger shows a widening gap in cost for greenery.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Minako, so a wetland might be safer to build and last longer than a plaza?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It would solve the drainage and heat, though we must ensure the tram commuters still have a clear path.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Minato,,"The volunteers are already experienced with habitat tasks, which helps the staffing shortage.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Minako,,It seems the most logical choice for longevity. Paving seems to be a waste of money here.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I still worry about the long-term budget, but the fund makes the initial phase viable.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm feeling positive about a nature-focused plan.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I agree, provided it doesn't block the main thoroughfare.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Minato,,I think the volunteers would be very happy.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Minako,,It is the most sustainable option based on the facts.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I can support that if the funding is structured correctly.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
